    "title": "Правила: Have been vs Have gone – Grammar Shorts",
    "level": "SHORTS",
    "overview": "Have been to и have gone to различаются тем, вернулся ли человек из места к reference time.",
    "main_rule": "Have been to = visited and returned. Have gone to = went there and is still away / not returned at reference time.",
    "form": "have/has been to + place. have/has gone to + place.",
    "when_why": "Для life experience → been to. Для current absence/presence elsewhere → gone to.",
    "examples": "I've been to London twice. → Я дважды был в Лондоне.\nSarah has gone to the supermarket. → Сара ушла в супермаркет.\nTom has been to Spain. → Том был в Испании.\nTom has gone to Spain. → Том уехал в Испанию и ещё не вернулся.",
    "special_cases": "Context decides whether person has returned.",
    "common_mistakes": "❌ I've gone to London twice. (если речь о past experience and return) → ✅ I've been to London twice.",
    "dont_confuse": "been to = visited and returned.\ngone to = went and is still away.",
    "quick_summary": "Experience → been.\nCurrently away → gone."
  },
